@node sotf-plugins Manual
@chapter Crate @code{sotf-plugins}
@cindex sotf-plugins

@code{sotf-plugins} is a facade crate that re-exports the host
(@code{sotf-host}) and every shipped DSP plugin
(@code{sotf-plugin-*}). It is the single dependency an application
needs to pull the whole plugin ecosystem.

@menu
* sotf-plugins User Guide::
* sotf-plugins Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node sotf-plugins User Guide
@section User Guide

@subheading What you get

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Core plugin system} (@code{sotf-host}): traits, DAG host,
  parameter system, analyser primitives.
@item @strong{Processing plugins}: 30+ DSP plugins as individual crates
  (EQ, dynamics, spatial, restoration, analysis -- see @ref{Plugins
  Reference}).
@item @strong{Analyser plugins}: spectrum analyser, EBU R128 loudness.
@item @strong{Plugin host}: DAG-based, parallel-safe.
@item @strong{Test utilities}: signal generators, allocation tracking,
  performance profilers.
@end itemize

@subheading Using a plugin from JSON

@example
PluginConfig @{
    plugin_type: "EQ".into(),
    parameters: json!(@{
        "filters": [
            @{ "filter_type": "peak",
              "frequency": 60.0, "q": 1.0, "gain_db": -4.0 @},
            @{ "filter_type": "highshelf",
              "frequency": 8000.0, "q": 0.7, "gain_db": 1.5 @}
        ]
    @})
@}
@end example

Plugins may change channel count (e.g.@: a stereo upmixer expands 2 to
5 channels); downstream plugins are configured accordingly.

@node sotf-plugins Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Workspace shape

@example
crates/sotf-plugins/
  src/lib.rs             facade: re-exports sotf-host + plugins
  Cargo.toml             depends on sotf-host + every sotf-plugin-*
  crates/
    sotf-host/           Plugin trait, DawHost, ParamSpec, analysers
    plugins-bridge/      common bridge code
    plugins-ffi/         C FFI surface
    plugins-au/          Audio Unit wrapper
    plugins-nih/         nih-plug bridge (CLAP / VST3)
    plugins-gpui/        GPUI editors shared across plugins
    plugins-denoiser/    shared denoiser building blocks
    plugins-spatial/     shared spatial building blocks
    sotf-plugin-*        one crate per plugin
@end example

@subheading Adding a plugin

@enumerate
@item Create @file{sotf-plugin-foo/} with @file{Cargo.toml} +
  @file{src/lib.rs}.
@item Add it to the workspace and to the facade's @file{Cargo.toml}.
@item Implement @code{Plugin} (see @ref{Plugin trait}).
@item Define a @code{pub const PARAMS: &[ParamSpec]} array.
@item Register the plugin in the host factory.
@item Add a unit test (golden buffer / property test).
@item Re-run @code{cargo run -p sotf-docs-gen} to regenerate the
  reference page.
@end enumerate

@subheading The three-places rule for parameters

@cindex parameter registration
A parameter must be wired in:

@enumerate
@item @code{rebuild_cached_parameters} (else silent rejection).
@item @code{set_parameter}.
@item @code{get_parameter}.
@end enumerate

Missing @code{rebuild_cached_parameters} is the most common cause of
"the slider does nothing".

@subheading Bridge crates

@table @code
@item plugins-nih
Wraps a SotF plugin behind @code{nih-plug} to produce CLAP and VST3
binaries.
@item plugins-au
Audio Unit (AUv3) wrapper. Uses @code{gpui-au} for the editor view.
@item plugins-ffi
Bare C ABI for embedding in other hosts.
@end table

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p sotf-plugins --no-default-features
@end example

Allocation regressions are caught by the allocation tracker in
@code{sotf-host} (@code{AllocTracker}); a failing test is a clear
signal that something is allocating in @code{process()}.
